{
  "slug": "jbm-harness-economics",
  "title": "The hidden cost of AI agents",
  "category": "AI costs",
  "summary": "An automated helper may consult its model many times before finishing a job. See what the meter counts, try a transparent example and compare selected published rates.",
  "reviewed": "2026-09-04",
  "reviewedLabel": "4 September 2026",
  "takeaways": [
    "The whole job can involve many paid requests.",
    "Caching changes how repeated input is billed; the first read still costs money.",
    "Compare the cost of successful work, not just a model’s token price."
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "harness",
      "title": "The model is one part of the job",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "The model proposes an answer or next action. Surrounding software supplies instructions, connects tools, tracks progress and decides whether to call the model again. Developers often call that software the harness. Like a cook working in a kitchen, a capable model needs a workflow around it; the workflow affects both results and cost.",
          "sources": [
            "loop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "flow",
          "title": "One job can involve repeated model calls",
          "steps": [
            "Read the task and available information",
            "Choose an answer or permitted action",
            "Use a tool and inspect its result",
            "Finish, ask for help or take another step"
          ],
          "note": "A conceptual agent loop. Actual systems may combine stages or stop at a budget limit.",
          "sources": [
            "loop"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "aliases": [
        "definition"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tokens",
      "title": "What the meter counts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "A token is a small piece of text used in processing and billing. It can be part of a word, a whole word or punctuation. Input includes instructions, documents, questions and earlier conversation. Output is generated material. Some systems also charge for reasoning that does not appear in the visible answer.",
          "sources": [
            "deepseek",
            "grokcache"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "The price cards use one million tokens as their unit. The calculator controls use thousands. Input and output have separate rates, so two requests with the same combined text size can cost different amounts. Subscriptions, tool calls, taxes and infrastructure can add charges outside a text-token calculation.",
          "sources": [
            "openai",
            "anthropic"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "aliases": [
        "loop"
      ]
    },
    {
