          "type": "p",
          "text": "With eight steps, 24,000 reference tokens and 2,000 reply tokens per step, total input is 248,000 tokens and output is 16,000. The reuse scenario contains 38,000 fresh input tokens and 210,000 reused tokens. Using Grok 4.6’s listed short-context rates gives $0.592 without caching and $0.277 with eligible reuse. These are arithmetic results from the stated assumptions.",
          "sources": [
            "grok"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "For N steps, C reference tokens and O reply tokens per step, total input is N × C + O × N × (N − 1) / 2. Total output is N × O. Every later step rereads the fixed reference plus all earlier replies. The first request has no reused input; each following request treats the latest reply as fresh.",
